<title>HONG KONG: Righteous year net loss HK$14.58 mln.</title>
<headline>Righteous year net loss HK$14.58 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended August 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.54 loss  vs 0.20 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	  vs 8.05 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    14.58 loss vs 1.88 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     243.24     vs 228.27</p>
<p>    Company name		 Righteous (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Righteous (Holdings) is a leather goods retailer.</p>
<p>During the year, the group closed all shops of a subsidiary which carried on retailing business of gold and diamond jewellery in Hong Kong. During the year and prior to the closure of those shops, the business had a turnover of approximately HK$38.59 million vs $45.86 million and an operating loss of approximately HK$4.21 million vs $5.33 million.</p>
<p>The turnover and the results of the business are therefore classified under discontinued operations. Comparative figures are reclassified accordingly.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
